d8a7ca-c38f-5c11-aa1b-651fc3654f5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128463" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-3,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨2,4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,3,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $p=⟨2,-3,5⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,3,-1⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,-3,5⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨1,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-128463/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128463"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33822/selection/dfb9eaaf79e6bc2a3fc0faf5dc710ff4283276a36d720f12041de81ef8a64bb5" :answer/id #uuid "af529e89-f16d-560a-bbc1-27393a0b40f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,-7,-8⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33822/selection/09d225066697f7e9777269ff31170ab0bf788ff48c4404cfd2f077529500ac62" :answer/id #uuid "0543e47d-e3ac-5ccd-9244-70eaf00bbafd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,13,-8⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33822/selection/a6276b69254e823566bd9694b85a18825e7d9253babb053cb88638ba50381f27" :answer/id #uuid "c26420c2-ef3b-5769-94eb-32335cd21d9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨13,3,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33822/selection/4958023f26edb902070c65569c7234080d07d8fd2dc06581195e272ce5bdbdcb" :answer/id #uuid "5277c0f7-53ef-5846-b406-7ea29a3181e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-5,1,1⟩" 