ese vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $E(16,-1,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $e=⟨16,-1,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =e+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨16,-1,3⟩+s⟨5,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,11,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70978/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70978"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33066"] :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $A(5,-3,1)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨8,1,0⟩+s⟨3,2,5⟩$ and $r=⟨6,-5,10⟩+t⟨0,6,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨3,2,5⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,6,2⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $A(5,-3,1)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $a=⟨5,-3,1⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨5,-3,1⟩+s⟨3,2,5⟩+t⟨0,6,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-128536/selection/c184d05b6347314e0ed7c9d6b754f3cdca4d11a47e55ff1c5ab75e8b24758c1b" :answer/id #uuid "27a50bf8-a41e-5c85-8ffc-2169a0be0b25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨-7,-3,12⟩+s⟨-3,4,2⟩+t⟨1,5,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128536/selection/29a3fc4bca7094b2df1852b5e9bbd80e86676a75a267db50b0a88a7ec6e9d06c" :answer/id #uuid "a020b529-7917-522b-8a10-d35ed66552f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨-7,-3,12⟩+s⟨3,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\