orked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-5,3,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,5,6⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(-7,12,-3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨-7,12,-3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128536/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128536"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128761/selection/a71914d18278de978479288e060b45d2247a6c728114fe99e476420b3153834f" :answer/id #uuid "78c7335c-4ef2-58db-a5b3-16c9383e696e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-5,4,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128761/selection/0cfaf7e526c250fbaee5a8c0263844d306fc79cb0c6812ce32f844065bdb0b1c" :answer/id #uuid "230f41a3-cb20-5c14-bcf0-a4340ef0c77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨-3,\\sqrt{5},2⟩+t⟨-4,2,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128761/selection/59a2af6bd7f06961f8c1ffd0cb86ee5ba8e82966deaa7c78603c82427d97f1c6" :answer/id #uuid "2c4ad019-fdba-579c-a342-c95728f303e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨2,\\sqrt{5},-3⟩+t⟨4,-2,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128761/selection/dd3298db23d2d84c50dc48fcbc7239c32dcb9dcd6e79191d7f9473258dffa99d" :answer/id #uuid "e56a2215-2acd-5880-87f1-f68dbae04c88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-2,4,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128761/selection/57ab4b45cbc8bffc301e3077f16ae29ca3d6a948946a0fedfdeee103d5e3f096" :answer/id #uuid "df3f3250-175c-5ecf-a7c1-be8bb5c22e53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-4,2,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128761/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2f11961-4564-5563-8db1-45242ab04039" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128761/selection/dd3298db23d2d84c50dc48fcbc7239c32dcb9dcd6e79191d7f9473258dffa99d" :answer-field/choices ["q-128761/selection/a71914d18278de978479288e060b45d2247a6c728114fe99e476420b3153834f" "q-128761/selection/0cfaf7e526c250fbaee5a8c0263844d306fc79cb0c6812ce32f844065bdb0b1c" "q-128761/selection/59a2af6bd7f06961f8c1ffd0cb86ee5ba8e82966deaa7c78603c82427d97f1c6" "q-128761/selection/dd3298db23d2d84c50dc48fcbc7239c32dcb9dcd6e79191d7f9473258dffa99d" "q-128761/selection/57ab4b45cbc8bffc301e3077f16ae29ca3d6a948946a0fedfdeee103d5e3f096"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128761" :question/id #uuid "35f4775a-5440-59b1-8bd7-3c5b1961d41e" :question/math-academy-id "q-128761" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(7,-3,4)$ and $Q(5,1,-1),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,1,-1⟩-⟨7,-3,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨7,-3,4⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-2,4,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-128761/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128761"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32988"] :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(3,1,5),\\,B(6,-8,0)$, and $C(-2,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨6,-8,0⟩-⟨3,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-9,-5⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨-2,1,3⟩-⟨3,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,0,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $a=⟨3,1,5⟩$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-33160/selection/e7648087cab0d366fca1170ed5bb1ac9b16095c4973db4d40cb8ab6c9f6ed144" :answer/id #uuid "c0d705d7-e3f3-592d-9715-3759af845b45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+s⟨1,4,-14⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33160/selection/9e60598870b10a2cfab0c4867985c6e860a96df5fea0fbafe3d5efcc27cc82c2" :answer/id #uuid "341ec3a4-5e5a-5e0d-9ff2-69ada5bfa505" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33160/selection/ca9808eaa63fece915ba2b04d8858c45b066c921a67038749918515c5c5dd9f2" :answer/id #uuid "47584619-4f06-5a98-9a74-9df914ff338a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,2,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33160/selection/8fea2a115138edb227db4bee0dd4322ee4d78878a498a6d1afba3af29b076200" :answer/id #uuid "f60f0621-8524-5cad-9a65-120927012eeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33160/selection/21c23afb400b5ecde4e1b3eb66e299e52cada41d68e41227ea75e59a02ad68a8" :answer/id #uuid "2ea2ac09-96b1-5b6b-af83-440a89eab687" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33160/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c443ab42-5f80-5b3e-b39f-f166702fbf8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33160/selection/8fea2a115138edb227db4bee0dd4322ee4d78878a498a6d1afba3af29b076200" :answer-field/choices ["q-33160/selection/e7648087cab0d366fca1170ed5bb1ac9b16095c4973db4d40cb8ab6c9f6ed144" "q-33160/selection/9e60598870b10a2cfab0c4867985c6e860a96df5fea0fbafe3d5efcc27cc82c2" "q-33160/selection/ca9808eaa63fece915ba2b04d8858c45b066c921a67038749918515c5c5dd9f2" "q-33160/selection/8fea2a115138edb227db4bee0dd4322ee4d78878a498a6d1afba3af29b076200" "q-33160/selection/21c23afb400b5ecde4e1b3eb66e299e52cada41d68e41227ea75e59a02ad68a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33160" :question/id #uuid "4253076c-f9b0-59ce-9a1b-d5e4c0bbca87" :question/math-academy-id "q-33160" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(1,4,-14)$ and is parallel to the two distinct lines $r=⟨-1,5,7⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+t⟨-2,-2,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,1,1⟩,$ respectively.\nBut ${v}_{2}=-2{v}_{1}.$ So, our lines are parallel. \n\nDespite this fact, two distinct parallel lines still determine a plane. Now: \n\n- from the equation of the first line, we get the point $P$ with the position vector $p=⟨-1,5,7⟩$ that lies on it, and\n\n- from the equation of the second line, we get the point $Q$ with the position vector $q=⟨0,3,-19⟩$ that lies on it.\n\nThe vector $u=q-p$ will be parallel to the required plane. \n\nComputing the coordinates of $u,$  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨0,3,-19⟩-⟨-1,5,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-26⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}∦{v}_{1},$ we can find the equation of our plane.\n\nWe know that the point $C(1,4,-14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=⟨1,4,-14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+tu \\\\ r & =⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-33160/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33160"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128745/selection/79fef613c6e3a99331927188e6fbf1149f522e3aaf4004c3db6463d9c29830ac" :answer/id #uuid "96b18f8f-0e74-5b73-a205-349646b72522" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,0⟩+t⟨2,-3,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128745/selection/22a39728f2607c7d33d5cc975d84bfae757ec8b9abddb582bf4f363f56a411f1" :answer/id #uuid "831c178f-3859-5788-96ce-9dd071542a9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,-1⟩+t⟨2,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128745/selection/eef3c3e850b5785e10756a1d5784923157dbc62dfd442da2800993245da43fdf" :answer/id #uuid "854f7b98-c641-5836-b207-6028f32f1fdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,-1,1⟩+t⟨3,-1,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128745/selection/dddcea0a3ba59e7d95dec720660bd048593cdb2f664600a32d6f47f9d176eb85" :answer/id #uuid "458963d4-275c-5fe7-bb4e-cff7ba0ebf39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,0,-1⟩+t⟨-1,3,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128745/selection/38b429a37ea08586c373b763ff10c7c225e2d903ad7472f7a52798d947f5143d" :answer/id #uuid "6e1f89fb-fd91-5160-aa6e-58fbd5d3c600" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128745/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "74e2071b-83bc-5d79-991d-eb767f1d0b1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128745/selection/22a39728f2607c7d33d5cc975d84bfae757ec8b9abddb582bf4f363f56a411f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-128745/selection/79fef613c6e3a99331927188e6fbf1149f522e3aaf4004c3db6463d9c29830ac" "q-128745/selection/22a39728f2607c7d33d5cc975d84bfae757ec8b9abddb582bf4f363f56a411f1" "q-128745/selection/eef3c3e850b5785e10756a1d5784923157dbc62dfd442da2800993245da43fdf" "q-128745/selection/dddcea0a3ba59e7d95dec720660bd048593cdb2f664600a32d6f47f9d176eb85" "q-128745/selection/38b429a37ea08586c373b763ff10c7c225e2d903ad7472f7a52798d947f5143d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128745" :question/id #uuid "0a7f0779-a02e-54b4-a490-a401988e7022" :question/math-academy-id "q-128745" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $D(3,2,-1),\\,E(3,1,-2),$ and $F(5,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨3,1,-2⟩-⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨5,1,2⟩-⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $d=⟨3,2,-1⟩$ of the point $D,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =d+s\\overset{\\to }{DE}+t\\overset{\\to }{DF} \\\\ r & =⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,-1⟩+t⟨2,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-128745/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128745"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128760/selection/0ebcc25be95f95beab025f5497572b5c207ef0f81a1626dab5c60560a0448d6c" :answer/id #uuid "190189ce-b4a1-5c28-b4a6-84251bb0f27b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-6,2,4⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128760/selection/03370c702bb139b1666cb2e43cd94e06df3bbf9a1e5adec9fb9979e365874723" :answer/id #uuid "77f70ab9-df05-5d06-8368-1847ce4eb05b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128760/selection/47d82077091d483cf316331b019acf75722b5f8b210c06b5898cc5cdb4230ab2" :answer/id #uuid "94004271-92e2-5a26-9cc9-b798a13c8b93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-6,4,2⟩+t⟨4,-4,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128760/selection/da542330f73ad115ecebbcd66644cf57a50101731e2afea3801fc2a284b103a9" :answer/id #uuid "bb8dd248-653a-5444-a799-dc1b572980a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨4,2,6⟩+t⟨-4,-3,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128760/selection/35ef0c07375bb2e6306b9e3e76689a4c2d482bfb723de46fd0dc546c1407a6e9" :answer/id #uuid "8dfd55f1-d72c-53c3-940e-c30413943ebb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,4,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128760/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "efe908a8-da17-59c3-a7de-9fca8a1238e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128760/selection/03370c702bb139b1666cb2e43cd94e06df3bbf9a1e5adec9fb9979e365874723" :answer-field/choices ["q-128760/selection/0ebcc25be95f95beab025f5497572b5c207ef0f81a1626dab5c60560a0448d6c" "q-128760/selection/03370c702bb139b1666cb2e43cd94e06df3bbf9a1e5adec9fb9979e365874723" "q-128760/selection/47d82077091d483cf316331b019acf75722b5f8b210c06b5898cc5cdb4230ab2" "q-128760/selection/da542330f73ad115ecebbcd66644cf57a50101731e2afea3801fc2a284b103a9" "q-128760/selection/35ef0c07375bb2e6306b9e3e76689a4c2d482bfb723de46fd0dc546c1407a6e9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128760" :question/id #uuid "59e11878-2a74-52d6-b175-2dda09601ebd" :question/math-academy-id "q-128760" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(5,3,1)$ and $V(2,-1,-3),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨2,-1,-3⟩-⟨5,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨5,3,1⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-128760/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128760"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4940"] :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,2,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 17,3,15 \\rangle$  and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle 5,0,-8 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{p}+ s\\mathbf{b}+ t \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,5 \\rangle,$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 17,3,15 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle 5,0,-8 \\rangle.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-3,2,5⟩+s\\,⟨17,3,15⟩+t\\,⟨5,0,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5884"] :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}= \\langle -6,3, 2 \\rangle + t \\langle 4, 2, -1 \\rangle + s \\langle 4, -3, 2 \\rangle,\\qquad t,\\,s \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 4, 2, -1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{w} = \\langle 4, -3, 2 \\rangle$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i-12j-20k \\\\  & =⟨1,-12,-20⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 1, -12, -20 \\rangle.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4941"] :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are $\\mathbf{v_1}=\\langle  -1,7,2  \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}=\\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $C(2,50,-19)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 2,50,-19 \\rangle.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨2,50,-19⟩+s\\,⟨-1,7,2⟩+t\\,⟨2\\sqrt{3},9,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4942"] :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(-1,4,-3),$ $B(7,5,4),$ and $C(2,-2,8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,5,4⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,-2,8⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -1,4,-3 \\rangle$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,4,-3⟩+s⟨8,1,7⟩+t⟨3,-6,11⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** The form of the final equation depends on our choice of vectors and the point on the plane. We could have picked other vectors. Likewise, we could have chosen $B$ or $C$ instead of $A$ as our point on the plane. So, the answer is *not unique*!" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
